  "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/zen-browser/desktop/tarball/1.24.1b",
  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/zen-browser/desktop/zipball/1.24.1b",
  "body": "# Zen Stable Release\n\n\n## Security\n- https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/security/advisories/mfsa2026-123/\n\n## New Features\n- Updated to Firefox 159.0.1\n- New grain options have been added to the theme picker. You can cycle through different grain effects by clicking on the circle inside the dial.\n\n## Fixes\n- Fixed a command prompt window briefly appearing on Windows when Zen restarts to apply an update.\n- Fixed passkey sign-in failing on websites that share passkeys across related sites, such as Facebook and Instagram.\n- Fixed crashes on Windows that could occur with some antivirus or other security software installed, in some cases also leaving WebGL disabled.\n- Fixed red and blue colors appearing swapped on some websites that use WebGL on Linux, including video call background effects.\n- More bug fixes and improvements.\n\n## Changes\n- On macOS, icons on the UI will now start using SF Symbols.\n- The 'About Zen' window has been redesigned.\n- 'My Review Request' option for Pull Requests live folder now searches for 'user-review-requested:@me' instead of 'review-requested:@me'\n",
